&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;A culture of growth&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;With over 50 nationalities represented, we’re proud to welcome people of all backgrounds to our growing community, and we’re always finding new ways to help people feel welcomed and included. Here, you’ll have the tools, training and support you need to work in a way that suits you, learn new skills and reach your potential.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For a career where you can drive our business and shape your future, apply now.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netlify&#39;s engineering teams build the products, platforms, and infrastructure that empower millions of developers and builders to create, deploy, and scale modern web applications. From AI-powered workflows to edge infrastructure and developer experience, our engineering teams tackle challenges that directly shape how modern web applications are built and deployed. We’re hiring engineers at the senior and staff levels across multiple teams, spanning AI runners and workflow orchestration, accounts and billing, growth, developer experience, and platform engineering across compute, edge infrastructure, build systems, and observability. On our Experience team, we’re rethinking how people and agents interact with Netlify through our CLI, SDK, and APIs as more of our users arrive through agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for thoughtful, full-stack engineers who enjoy owning problems end to end, collaborating across disciplines, and solving complex technical challenges for products that millions of developers rely on every day. AI is a foundational part of how we build, so we value engineers who are excited to thoughtfully incorporate AI-assisted workflows while continuing to apply strong engineering fundamentals. As an engineer at Netlify, you’ll work alongside experienced engineers who care about building great software, sharing knowledge, and helping one another grow. We believe the best engineering happens when talented people are trusted to solve difficult problems together, share what they&#39;re learning, and create space for different perspectives to shape better solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With our team, you&#39;ll have real ownership from day one - not a tiny slice of a massive codebase. Engineers here are trusted to make decisions, shape technical direction, and move quickly while collaborating closely with Product and Design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use your expertise in full-stack development (Our stack is TypeScript/JavaScript, React, Ruby, and Go) to ship reliable, scalable, performant code across our product suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain user-facing features, product APIs, and platform capabilities that scale to support millions of developers worldwide and lead projects from conception to delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply strong engineering fundamentals, including testing, documentation, observability, and performance optimization, while thoughtfully incorporating AI-assisted development tools to accelerate prototyping, experimentation, and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate ambiguity with curiosity, contributing to both early-stage prototypes and production-ready applications that directly improve the developer experience and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practice proactive async communication and create visibility across projects by documenting your workflows and decision-making clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews, on-call rotations, and continuous improvement efforts to reduce technical debt and maintain high engineering standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate regularly with Engineering, Product, Design, and cross-functional teammates to design and implement experiences that help developers build faster and more effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with teammates to share knowledge, mentor others through collaboration, and contribute to a thoughtful, inclusive engineering culture where continuous learning is encouraged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated engineering proficiency with a curiosity for building with new technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong full-stack expertise, with experience developing and maintaining production-quality software in modern full-stack environments. Required familiarity with one of the following: TypeScript and JavaScript, Go or Ruby for backend services and API development. Broader familiarity preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive production experience delivering features and services that serve large user bases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing high-quality, testable code that&#39;s reliable and maintainable over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI-assisted development tools (such as GitHub Copilot, Claude, Cursor, GPT-based agents, or similar technologies) to build applications, improve engineering workflows, or accelerate software development, along with good judgment about when and how to apply them effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical thinking abilities and a solution-oriented approach to complex technical challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to participate in an on-call rotation after onboarding, responding primarily to scaling and reliability incidents using established runbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach to problem-solving with curiosity about how your work supports teammates, users, and broader company goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth mindset and openness to learning new tools, technologies, and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for working in a collaborative environment with teammates across distributed locations, and strong written and verbal communication skills, especially in asynchronous, remote-first environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This Role is a Great Fit If&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re energized by building products and platform capabilities that help millions of developers create, deploy, and scale applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You see ambiguity as a creative opportunity and enjoy solving problems where there isn&#39;t always a predefined path forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You see AI as a multiplier for your engineering skills - not a shortcut - and can thoughtfully articulate where it adds value, where it doesn&#39;t, and how you use it responsibly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy owning problems from end to end and are motivated by opportunities to make meaningful technical and product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working autonomously and making decisions within a distributed, async, remote-first team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re excited by new tools, challenges, and opportunities to grow, even when they feel a little uncomfortable at first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You value curiosity, continuous learning, and creating an environment where teammates can learn from one another and do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You want to work on a fully remote team that believes in autonomy, transparency, inclusion, and building a better web, together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applying&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not sure you meet 100% of our qualifications? &lt;strong&gt;Please apply anyway!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When applying please include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A resume or short listing of your job history &amp;amp; skills (link to a LinkedIn profile would be fine). We appreciate a cover letter explaining why you would enjoy working in this role at Netlify to get to know you a bit better, though this is not required and will not impact your application. Our mission is to “build a better web” and that cannot be done without a diversity of skill sets, backgrounds and thoughts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Of everything we&#39;ve ever built at Netlify, we are most proud of our team. Netlify is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are devoted to building a team of people with diverse backgrounds and lifestyles. Driving equality empowers our team, enables us to innovate, and helps us maintain a more inclusive environment. We don’t discriminate against employees or applicants based on gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, age, race, military/veteran status, citizenship, pregnancy status, or any other differences. If we can do anything to provide a better interview, i.e. accommodate a disability, then please let us know by emailing accommodations@netlify.com.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Netlify&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Netlify is the most popular way to build, deploy and scale modern web applications. Home to millions of developers and thousands of enterprises, Netlify is the platform of choice for running modern composable web applications in production, from global corporate sites to complex e-commerce and SaaS applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a Series D company that has raised over $200M from investors such as Andreessen Horowitz, Kleiner Perkins, EQT, Bessemer, BOND, and Menlo Ventures. As a fully distributed company, we aim to create a company culture where the best idea can come from anywhere and strive to be thoughtful, compassionate, and collaborative in our work. If this sounds like something you’d like to be part of, we’re excited to connect with you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Netlify, we are committed to a compensation philosophy that prioritizes fairness and equity, positions our employee compensation competitively in the market, recognizes and rewards performance, and takes a comprehensive approach to our rewards package. We anchor our compensation philosophy on a market-based approach, therefore salary ranges may differ depending on the labor cost in a particular location. The salary provided is in addition to robust benefits and participation in Netlify’s equity plan. Our hiring range for this role is targeted at $148,000 - $180,000 for most US-based locations, $131,000 - $192,000 CAD in most Canada-based locations, £84,000 – £114,000 GBP for most UK-based locations, and €63,000 - €86,000 EUR in most Spain-based locations. &amp;nbsp;Candidates outside the US, Canada, Spain, or in premium markets should consult with their Talent Acquisition partner regarding location-based ranges, as they may be higher or lower than the average US range listed. The starting pay will be determined based on multiple factors, including expertise and skills, market demands, experience, internal equity, and applicable geographic location. These compensation packages and ranges are subject to change and may be modified in the future.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Senior Manager, Solutions Architecture - at GitLab, you&#39;ll manage a distributed team of Solutions Architects working with customers across AMER. In this player-coach role, you&#39;ll guide technical strategy across complex sales motions while also stepping directly into high-impact opportunities to help your team secure technical wins and build customer confidence in GitLab&#39;s platform approach. At GitLab, we work at the intersection of technical sales strategy, team development, and operational scale, and you&#39;ll help translate customer requirements into clear business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with regional go-to-market counterparts and cross-functional teams including Sales, Channel, Marketing, Sales Enablement, Product Management, and the global Solutions Architecture team. In our all-remote environment, you&#39;ll help shape how we grow the Solutions Architecture organization across the region by building strong operating rhythms, strengthening executive relationships, and creating the conditions for your team to do their best work. This role suits someone who combines technical depth, strong judgment, and a hands-on approach to winning business and scaling teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some of the types of projects you&#39;ll work on:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running technical evaluations, executive workshops, demos, and proof-of-concept engagements that help customers map GitLab&#39;s DevSecOps platform to their business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a team of intermediate and senior Solutions Architects across AMER setting clear direction and enabling high-quality execution across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a player-coach by partnering directly on strategic opportunities, building executive relationships, and coaching your team through complex sales cycles to help secure the technical win.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide regional strategy for technical evaluations, workshops, demonstrations, and proof-of-concept engagements, ensuring customer needs are translated into meaningful technical and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with global Solutions Architecture, Sales, Channel, Marketing, Sales Enablement, and Product Management to align on priorities and execute against regional goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage dotted-line relationships with Channel Solutions Architects and subject matter experts, driving accountability, collaboration, and alignment around common goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong operational discipline across workload planning, resource allocation, headcount planning, opportunity forecasting, and field execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track key performance indicators for the team, communicating progress, risks, and priorities clearly to your team, peers, and senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, develop, and retain high-performing Solutions Architects while strengthening team capability, encouraging innovation, and building a scalable regional organization for future growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consumption experience: The ability to assess technical depth and consumption capability across a team and to build the talent system that improves both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical experience: A credible hands-on background in solution architecture, and the ability to set expectations for architecture and deployment quality across cloud, hybrid and on-premises or self-managed environments for your region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of consumption economics, regional pipeline dynamics and adoption patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of how forecast assumptions, usage risk and POV quality shape regional performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in calibration frameworks for assessing consumption-based sales experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to turn deal-level patterns into regional programs and playbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to spot forecast and adoption risk early and act at the system level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to coach managers on partnering with commercial leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivation to build managers who coach the consumption motion well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Energy for making regional results predictable and repeatable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to a consistent, fair, evidence-based hiring bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel at least 25%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Solutions Architecture team sits within GitLab Sales and partners with Account Executives, Customer Success and Product to help customers adopt GitLab and grow their usage over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We act as technical advisors across the full software delivery lifecycle: DevOps, CI/CD, cloud-native platforms, security and software supply chain, and AI-native development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab sells in a consumption-based model, so our work does not end at the proof of value. We map how customers will use GitLab, prove value with evidence, and stay close through production adoption and expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We share what we learn, coach each other, and care about measurable customer outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
